{"id": "EUVD-2026-81708", "enisaUuid": "25c13def-8f83-3851-a0ff-5b557e8dfae0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxsk: fix NULL pointer dereference in __xsk_rcv()\n\nIn the __xsk_rcv() multi-buffer path, xsk_buff_alloc() is called in a\nloop without checking its return value. xsk_buff_can_alloc() only\ncounts fill queue entries without validating their addresses, so it\ncan succeed while xsk_buff_alloc() rejects all remaining entries and\nreturns NULL.\n\n  Oops: general protection fault, probably for non-canonical address\n   0xdffffc0000000000\n  KASAN: null-ptr-deref in range\n   [0x0000000000000000-0x0000000000000007]\n  RIP: 0010:__xsk_rcv+0x426/0xc20 (net/xdp/xsk.c:350)\n  Call Trace:\n   xsk_generic_rcv+0x26d/0x5f0\n   xdp_do_generic_redirect+0x3c5/0xcf0\n   do_xdp_generic+0x92f/0xe70\n   __netif_receive_skb_core.constprop.0+0xf7e/0x2b30\n\nFix this with a two-stage transaction. First allocate and stage all\nbuffers required for the packet, recycling all staged buffers with\nxsk_buff_free() if any allocation fails. Only after this stage\nsucceeds, copy the data, reserve the RX descriptors, and release the\nbuffers in an error-free loop.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:58:13", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aaebce297efc3e3dccb98a6ff838cfaa47db08db", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/60d7d3559ce66e227e195e9463cdfed8077c8659", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/214fb79b0379cb0214905632a2537c0c33f594eb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8341bd3ff126d85bc8c4ed52eedcaa5b1a65f194", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e37b2abca80473e106176e41712a369fd2f72117"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fwqw-j57j-h6cj", "CVE-2026-90115"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "052da597-1d7e-3a56-8c07-90a5b23d9c62", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "18e45bcf-675e-309b-a642-c597ff68de5d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "1ab81199-63fe-378f-b27c-125a6c2ceec6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "265198b5-aff4-3719-97c4-a25bd813fcd3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "804627751b4281dd95148e7564759145da67855e <214fb79b0379cb0214905632a2537c0c33f594eb"}, {"id": "2b9c1a02-aaed-37ca-8a33-4e3c78b06c8c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "804627751b4281dd95148e7564759145da67855e <e37b2abca80473e106176e41712a369fd2f72117"}, {"id": "2f8849b1-1c44-3f92-83cf-531601256a8b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6b192e03-3764-3e9b-b87e-38a3eb1f46d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "7b74da82-9487-31a6-9339-a0bf95f9db49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "804627751b4281dd95148e7564759145da67855e <60d7d3559ce66e227e195e9463cdfed8077c8659"}, {"id": "84d194a6-e6da-3a52-9d91-43bdf615f8c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "b110db12-1222-3385-aed7-124e8e109f08", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "804627751b4281dd95148e7564759145da67855e <8341bd3ff126d85bc8c4ed52eedcaa5b1a65f194"}, {"id": "be8dbe60-edb4-3108-a21d-30fd27369817", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "d5a7224e-853b-371e-91e9-722d885ad281", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "804627751b4281dd95148e7564759145da67855e <aaebce297efc3e3dccb98a6ff838cfaa47db08db"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "263170b3-3fb5-3d95-a9f1-ff4428fdd4dd", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}